1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:04,580
Good morning. World Tours. My name is Jamie. How can I help you?

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:09,930
Good morning. I want some information on self-drive tours in the USA.

3
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:11,600
Could you send me a brochure?

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,940
Of course. Could I have your name please?

5
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:15,600
Andrea Brown.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,080
Thank you. And your address?

7
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,550
24. Ardleigh Road.

8
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:21,760
Can you spell that?

9
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:27,040
A-R-D-L-E. I-G-H Road.

10
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,080
Postcode?

11
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:34,710
BH520P Thanks. And can I have your phone number?

12
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,200
Is a mobile alright?

13
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:36,760
Fine.

14
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:44,080
It's 07786643091.

15
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:47,737
Thank you. And can I ask you where you heard about World Tours?

16
00:00:47,737 --> 00:00:50,550
From a friend? Or did you see an advert somewhere?

17
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,180
No, I read about you in the newspaper.

18
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:56,120
OK, I'll get the brochures in the post to you

19
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,350
but can I give you some information over the phone.

20
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,500
What kinds of things do you want to do on your holiday?

21
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,060
I'm interested in going to California with my family

22
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,640
I've got two children and we want to hire a car.

23
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:14,750
OK. We have a couple of self-drive tours there visiting different places of interest in California.

24
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:17,180
The first one begins in Los Angeles

25
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:20,150
and there's plenty of time to visit some of the theme parks there.

26
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:24,620
That's something on my children's list so I'd want to include that.

27
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:27,540
Good. Then you drive to San Francisco.

28
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:31,060
From San Francisco you can drive to Yosemite Park

29
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,920
where you spend a couple of nights.

30
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:36,400
You can choose to stay in a lodge or on the campsite.

31
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,700
I don't like the idea of staying in a tent. It'd be too hot.

32
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,630
Right. And the tour ends in Las Vegas.

33
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:44,480
OK.

34
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,774
The other trip we can arrange is slightly different.

35
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:51,800
It starts in San Francisco. Then you drive south to Cambria.

36
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:57,310
Someone told me there's a really nice castle near Cambria. Will we go near that?

37
00:01:57,310 --> 00:02:00,500
Hearst Castle is on that road so you could stop there.

38
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:05,620
Good. I'd like to do that. Does this trip also go into the desert?

39
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:07,820
No, it continues to Santa Monica

40
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,440
where most people like to stop and do some shopping.

41
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:14,370
We have enough of that at home so that doesn't interest us.

42
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:18,160
OK. Well, you could go straight on to San Diego.

43
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,350
That's good for beaches isn't it?

44
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:23,160
That's right, that's a good place to relax

45
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:26,120
and your children might like to visit the zoo before flying home.

46
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:32,750
I don't think so. We want some time for sunbathing and swimming.

47
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:37,100
So how many days are the trips and how much do they cost?

48
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:42,720
The first one I told you about is a self-drive tour through California

49
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:46,610
which lasts twelve days and covers 2,020 kilometres.

50
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:50,240
The shortest journey is 206 km

51
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:57,510
and the longest is 632 kilometres. The cost is 525 per person.

52
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:02,180
That includes accommodation, car rental and a flight but no meals.

53
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,520
OK. And the other trip?

54
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:08,720
That lasts nine days but you spend only three days on the road

55
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:11,770
You cover about 980 kilometres altogether.

56
00:03:11,770 --> 00:03:13,550
So is that cheaper then?

57
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:15,840
Yes, it's almost a hundred pounds cheaper

58
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:19,410
It's 429 per person, which is a good deal.

59
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:24,710
So that covers accommodation and car hire. What about flights?

60
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:28,580
They aren't included. But these hotels offer dinner in the price.

61
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,400
OK. Well, thank you very much

62
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,450
I'll be in touch when I've had a chance to look at the brochure.

63
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:36,330
I'm pleased to help. Goodbye.

64
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:37,000
Goodbye.
